# --- Rust ------------------------------------------------------------------
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS committed. This crate produces a binary, and for binaries a
# committed lockfile is what makes a build reproducible. (Libraries omit it.)

# --- not for publication ----------------------------------------------------
# Keyrock's own hiring material; the repo is public.
docs/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- local working material, deliberately not part of the deliverable ------
# Agent scaffolding and personal working notes. These are how the work gets
# done, not the work itself; the reviewer gets the code, the tests, and the
# README.
#
# specs/ is NOT in this list, on purpose: unlike the rest of this block, the
# spec packets (inputs/spec.md/plan.md/tasks.md per step) are tracked and
# committed, so the commit history shows the reasoning behind each step
# alongside the code it produced.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
NOTES.md
scratch/

